cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenTherm: A Unified and Progressive Benchmark for 2.5D/3D-IC Thermal Prediction"
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark for 2.5D/3D-IC thermal prediction that combines 32,000
  established 3D-IC samples with 50,000 new HotSpot-generated 2.5D chiplet
  samples, fixed splits, a common input representation, and shared evaluation
  tools. Five Generalization Scopes cover fixed-design workload prediction,
  within-family layout, material, and cooling exploration, and cross-package
  out-of-distribution transfer with few-shot adaptation. The released code
  trains, evaluates, and adapts eight model configurations from one entry point.
  Previously released as IC-ThermBench.
